course: dictionary
lesson: 5505
title: Layoff: when jobs end
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A layoff happens when a company stops employing workers, often because there is not enough work or money. Use the clues around the word to check. «The factory made mass layoffs after the orders dried up» tells you that many people lost their jobs because there was less work.
explain: The words around a word can warn you what it means. «The company sent a layoff notice to every worker on Monday.» A notice is a message, so a layoff notice is a message telling workers their jobs will end. Nobody sends that message as a treat.
explain: Writers sometimes use softer words to make hard news sound gentler. «Let go» is one of these phrases, and it means the same as a layoff. Business writers may also say «workforce adjustment». When you read this kind of news, ask yourself: did people lose their jobs?
fact: A layoff means a company stops employing workers, often because there is not enough work or money.
fact: «Mass layoffs» means many workers lost their jobs at the same time.
fact: A «layoff notice» is a message telling workers that their jobs will end.
fact: In sport, a layoff is a time when a player is not playing, often because of an injury.
fact: «Let go» and «workforce adjustment» are softer ways to say layoffs. A euphemism is a gentler word used for something hard.
exercise: «The factory made mass layoffs after the orders dried up.» What does mass layoffs mean? | * Many workers lost their jobs at the same time | Many workers were given extra pay | Nobody was allowed to go home | The factory was built in one day
exercise: In a sports report, a player is out on a long layoff with an injury. What does layoff mean here? | * A time when the player is not playing | A long run around the pitch | A new job as a coach | A goal scored from a corner
exercise: Which phrase is a softer way of saying that workers have lost their jobs? | Pay rise | * Let go | Gold star | Extra holiday
test: «The bank issued a layoff notice to its staff this morning.» What does the notice most likely tell the staff? | They have won a prize | Their pay is going up | The bank is closing for a holiday | * Their jobs are ending
test: Business writers call layoffs «workforce adjustment». What does that phrase mean? | Workers choosing new hobbies | Workers getting a new office | Workers taking a long holiday | * Workers losing their jobs
exam: Why do writers sometimes say «let go» instead of layoff? | To make the word shorter for young readers | To mean a different kind of job | To make the news sound more exciting | * To make hard news sound gentler
